tput .signpost-subscription .sidebar-below a{color:var(--color-subtle,#777)}.mw-parser-output .signpost-subscription-general{border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding:5px 0;margin-top:5px;font-size:95%}@media(min-width:720px){.mw-parser-output .signpost-subscription{width:23em}.mw-parser-output .signpost-subscription-left{float:left}.mw-parser-output .signpost-subscription-none{float:none}} 13 October 2026 hide News and notes: AELECT returns, Jimbo gives a union update, VisualEditor is now defaultPlus a survey for North Americans, proposed changes to BoT elections, and developments in the Puerto Rican editing community. Serendipity: From a rare portrait of a female millionaire in Nancy to a Japanese painter in LyonImages from Leuven Libraries popular on Wiki. Obituary: Doug WellerTwenty-year editor, long-term admin, dearly missed. In the media: A(I)pocalypses afootCannibals, freeloaders, rogue agents, scams ... the usual. WikiConference Report: WikiConference 2026 & the importance of in-person communityCelebrating 12 years of WikiConference North America. By the numbers: Does the country of birth affect the likelihood of having a Wikipedia biography?A cross-country and cross-wikipedia comparison of the likelihood of having a biography in Wikipedia. News from Diff: OpenAI "rogue" agent activities found on Wikimedia projectsCPO/CTO Selena Deckelmann explains the recent detection of AI agent activities on Wikimedia projects. On the bright side: Good peopleNice comments and real-life rescuers. Op-ed: Who are our readers?The movement makes progress when we know what our scope is. Traffic report: This world is big and wild and half insaneCriminals, 9/11 25 years later, artists expelled for politics... we lived in troubled times. Comix: Fudging the numbersTake 'em away, officers! Single page Front page About Subscribe Suggestions Archives @213,4267,471,2030
